<urn:atm:triage:finding/S9-CI-WIN-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "S9-CI-WIN-002" ;
  triage:title "Windows compile failure — LocalEnvSet and LocalEnvGuard::set_many ungated, dead code on Windows" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-core/src/home.rs test module — LocalEnvGuard::set_many() method (line 285) and LocalEnvSet struct (line 311) plus its Drop impl (line 331) are defined unconditionally but only called from #[cfg(unix)]-gated tests. On Windows: '-D warnings' compile failure with 'associated function set_many is never used' and 'struct LocalEnvSet is never constructed'. CI-WIN-001 fix resolved the OsString E0425 error; CI-WIN-002 is a new dead-code lint failure caught by 'just lint' clippy on Windows. Fix: add #[cfg(unix)] gate to LocalEnvSet struct definition, its Drop impl, and LocalEnvGuard::set_many method. All callers are already #[cfg(unix)]-gated." ;
  triage:category "CI" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
